-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">First-Time Buyers &middot; Myrtle Beach, SC</p>
-<h1 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3rem);color:var(--navy);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:1.1rem;letter-spacing:-.02em">Your first home in Myrtle Beach may take less cash than you think.</h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Chapter3 Realty &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 27, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">What a first-time buyer can afford in Myrtle Beach, the down-payment help South Carolina offers, and the condo and inland-house entry points most first-timers start with.</p>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:700px;margin-bottom:1.8rem">Buying your first home on the Grand Strand is not like buying your first home anywhere else. You are competing with out-of-state cash buyers, working through bylaws and insurance that surprise first-timers. This page covers what matters, and how to find out what you qualify for in one phone call.</p>
-<div style="display:flex;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
-<a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Talk to a local agent</a>
-
-</div>
-</div>
-</section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">What you can afford here</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">The most attainable ways into the Grand Strand market</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Oceanfront is not a starter home, and it does not have to be. For most first-time buyers on the Grand Strand, the realistic entry points are condos, townhomes, and single-family starter homes inland. Inland includes <a href="/submarkets/conway/">Conway</a>, parts of Carolina Forest, and the neighborhoods a few miles back from the beach. Our guide to the <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places to buy a home near Myrtle Beach</a> compares the inland towns. With a condo or townhome, watch the HOA fee and whether the building is lender-approved. A fourth entry point suits a buyer willing to be a landlord on day one. An owner-occupied loan works on a <a href="/invest/strategies/small-multifamily/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">duplex, triplex or fourplex</a> when you live in one of the units, and the other rents help pay the loan. Prices climb the closer you get to the water.</p>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A large share of Grand Strand buyers are paying cash from out of state, which surprises first-timers. That means a clean pre-approval and an agent who can move fast matter more here than in a lot of markets. Our <a href="/submarkets/">neighborhood guides</a> break down what each town looks like for people buying a home to live in.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The one-roof advantage</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How financing fits in</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Chapter3 works alongside an affiliated preferred lender, so your pre-approval, your offer, and your closing are handled by one team that talks to each other. For a first-time buyer that means fewer dropped balls, and straight answers on the tricky stuff, like whether a specific condo building is actually financeable, or how a condotel loan works, before you fall in love with a place you can't get a loan on. (See our Affiliated Business Arrangement disclosure in the footer for how that relationship works.)</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">What surprises buyers here?</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">First-time buyer mistakes specific to Myrtle Beach</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A few Grand Strand realities first-time buyers routinely miss:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1.2rem;padding-left:1.2rem;display:grid;gap:.55rem"><li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Flood zones.</strong> Flood insurance can add real monthly cost, so check the zone before you fall for a house.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Wind and hail.</strong> Near the coast this is often a separate policy from your regular homeowners insurance.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Condo costs.</strong> The building's master insurance, HOA fees, and special assessments can change the math overnight.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you write an offer, we pull the HOA bylaws, budget, reserve study, and financials so there are no surprises. Your lender will usually require only hazard insurance, plus flood insurance if the home is in a flood zone.</p>
-<p style="margin-bottom:0"><a href="/buyers/common-mistakes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Common buyer mistakes on the Grand Strand &rarr;</a> &nbsp; <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">How buying in Myrtle Beach works &rarr;</a></p>
-</div></section>
